From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:11:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] egl: reach zink on platforms without DRM devices

The surfaceless platform only falls back to its DRM-less probe when software
rendering is forced, so a platform with no DRM devices at all, such as Apple,
could never reach zink: the hardware probe finds no device node and the
retry in eglInitialize clears the zink request before forcing software. Take
the DRM-less probe when zink is requested as well, where it selects zink
through kopper rather than a software rasterizer.
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
index e85cae5d61b7f5c99972bcaaf545daa040ee38fd..e1ca89213c78c61d0df8953b4daf4cd2df3c148d 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
@@ -389,7 +389,8 @@ dri2_initialize_surfaceless(_EGLDisplay *disp)
     */
    driver_loaded = surfaceless_probe_device(disp, disp->Options.ForceSoftware,
                                             disp->Options.Zink);
-   if (!driver_loaded && disp->Options.ForceSoftware) {
+   if (!driver_loaded && (disp->Options.ForceSoftware || disp->Options.Zink)) {
+      /* Platforms without DRM devices, such as Apple, reach zink only here. */
       _eglLog(_EGL_DEBUG, "Falling back to surfaceless swrast without DRM.");
       driver_loaded = surfaceless_probe_device_sw(disp);
    }
